body:
Builds the P0 architecture and a real binary activation data plane across logical nodes.

Architecture and terminology:

- `jetsonfabric-runtime-worker` is the JetsonFabric-owned runtime host; inference engines are hosted adapters such as `llama.cpp` and the CI-only `synthetic` engine;
- stage position is derived from `stage_index` and `stage_count`, with no stage-role string;
- route metadata uses objective topology and stage/host counts;
- automatic placement and layer-range arithmetic are count-aware and centrally validated;
- `internal/inference` owns engine-neutral prefill/decode lifecycle and legal payload transitions;
- `internal/stagewire` owns the versioned cross-stage binary contract;
- `internal/stageexec` owns ordered stage invocation and binary handoff;
- `internal/runtimebridge` streams frames between node APIs and node-local runtimes;
- legacy `internal/layersplit` and `internal/routing` planning paths are removed.

Stagewire v1:

- media type `application/vnd.jetsonfabric.stage.v1+octet-stream`;
- fixed 20-byte `JFST`/version/flags/length header;
- UTF-8 JSON metadata followed by raw payload bytes;
- no base64 and no JSON tensor arrays;
- payload kinds: `text`, `tokens`, `activation`, and `sampled_token`;
- tensor metadata: dtype, shape, little-endian byte order, and row-major layout;
- CRC32, length, version, size, truncation, trailing-data, and tensor-shape validation;
- matching Go and C++ frame implementations.

Activation proof:

- synthetic stage 0 emits a deterministic `f32[4,16]` activation;
- the activation crosses two real logical-node APIs and two supervised C++ runtime workers;
- stage 1 validates the activation and returns its CRC32 as a `u32[1]` sampled-token payload;
- stage traces assert activation byte-length and checksum continuity across the logical-node boundary.

Current limitation:

- the existing `llama.cpp` path still performs full-model generation at each stage;
- real partial-layer activations, persistent stage-local KV state, and the coordinator decode loop remain subsequent milestones.

Validation:

- `go test ./...`;
- native C++ runtime build;
- real two-node `llama.cpp` CPU E2E;
- real two-node synthetic binary-activation E2E;
- one `CI` workflow and one sequential `CI` job.
